# Zenkai LAUNCH env — fill the <> values, then:
#   scp ops/env.launch.template zenkai@<box-ip>:Zenkai/.env
#
# Sized for a public launch on a CPX31 (4 vCPU AMD / 8GB / 160GB, Ashburn),
# not the ten-person beta the first draft assumed. Differences from that
# draft are called out inline.

# --- keys -----------------------------------------------------------------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<sk-ant-...>
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=<voice; omit and sessions run text-only>

# --- public identity ------------------------------------------------------
IP_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://zenkai.run
IP_PUBLIC_SESSION_URL=https://session.zenkai.run
IP_APP_BIND=127.0.0.1

# --- auth (Supabase) ------------------------------------------------------
IP_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
IP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon key — safe in the browser>
IP_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=<service role key — server only, reaches NO child process>
IP_AUTH_ADMIN_EMAILS=zhang4021@gmail.com
# IP_SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=   # only for legacy HS256 projects; new ones use JWKS

# --- concurrency ----------------------------------------------------------
IP_MULTI_SESSION=1
# Raised 4 -> 8 for launch. The box (4 vCPU / 8GB, no swap) has headroom: a room
# is ~28MB idle, ~200MB-1GB active, and CPU is shared dynamically (no per-session
# pinning), so contention degrades to latency, not failure. RAM is the real
# ceiling — watch `docker stats` on the first busy evening. The idle reaper below
# keeps these 8 slots actually available instead of clogged by abandoned tabs.
IP_MAX_CONCURRENT_SESSIONS=8
IP_MAX_SESSIONS_PER_USER=1
# Session slot reaper (session.ts reapReason). A live round frees its slot when
# its tab has been gone this long (no /api/status heartbeat), or when the round
# has run this long absolutely. Unset = the code defaults shown here. A silent
# reader is NOT reaped — the open tab keeps polling every 3s.
# IP_SESSION_IDLE_MS=900000     # 15 min idle -> reap (abandoned tab)
# IP_SESSION_MAX_MS=5400000     # 90 min absolute -> reap (untimed-round backstop)

# --- sample round (the activation door) ------------------------------------
# The rep whose pristine archive seeds the free "try the sample" round on the
# home page — what a first visitor plays before signing up for anything. If
# unset, sampleArchivePath() returns null: the card never renders and
# /api/practice/sample 404s. It is NON-secret config and MUST live here (not a
# hand-set repo .env line) or push-env drops it — which is exactly what broke it
# on 2026-08-21. Value is a rep id under reps/<id> with a problem.pristine.tar.gz.
IP_SAMPLE_REP=rep-msxg6yev

# --- generation throughput + spend ----------------------------------------
# RAISED FROM 1 for launch. At 1, builds serialize globally: five people
# arriving in an hour means the fifth waits ~25 minutes seeing "someone
# else's round is generating." At 2 they mostly don't collide, and 2
# concurrent opus runs still leave CPU for live rooms on 4 vCPU.
#
# SPEND CEILING, READ THIS: each build is a ~5-minute agentic opus run. Two
# concurrent builds is a theoretical ~576 builds/day. Nothing in the product
# caps global daily spend — the real throttles are this number, the per-user
# caps below, and Google's 100-test-user ceiling. Watch the Anthropic console
# for the first few days; if traffic is real, a global daily build cap is a
# small follow-up.
IP_MAX_CONCURRENT_BUILDS=2
IP_MAX_REPS_PER_USER_DAY=3
IP_MAX_PENDING_REPS_PER_USER=4
# GLOBAL builds/day across ALL users — the ONLY cap a fresh email cannot reset,
# so it is the real backstop under the $1000/mo Anthropic ceiling. A build is
# ~$1.35-$4.39, so 40 caps a bad day near ~$120 and trips well before a farming
# loop matters. Drop to 20 (~$60/day worst case) if you would rather never risk
# a mid-month blackout; raise it once you have watched a real busy evening.
IP_MAX_BUILDS_PER_DAY=40
# Per-user daily caps on the two model doors that mint no rep row (app.ts
# dailyUserCount). Unset falls back to the code defaults shown here.
IP_MAX_PLANNER_TURNS_PER_DAY=60
IP_MAX_CLARIFY_RUNS_PER_DAY=30

# --- retention ------------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules reaped once a round is graded (60MB -> ~2MB); used reps slimmed
# after 14 days; unconsumed work is NEVER age-reaped.
IP_RETENTION_DAYS=14
IP_REAP_NODE_MODULES=1

# --- willingness-to-pay gate (paywall.ts) ---------------------------------
# THIS ONE REALLY DENIES. Past the free allowance a user is shown a price and
# does not get that round unless they press Subscribe. No card details are
# collected anywhere — the measurement is the click, and the reveal that
# payments are not switched on yet is immediate and in place.
#
# KILL SWITCH: comment IP_PAYWALL_GATE out and
#   sudo systemctl restart zenkai-app
# ~10 seconds, and KillMode=process means nobody's live round is touched.
# One bad report from a beta user turns the whole thing off, no deploy.
#
# You are exempt (admin), so you will never see it on the live box. To eyeball
# the flow run this in the devtools console:
#   showPaywallGate({price_usd:39, reason:'rounds', used:3, free:3})
#
# 3 rounds is the experiment; 3 plans is a guardrail, not the measurement (a
# plan costs ~$1 against a round's $1.35-$4.39, and it is the on-ramp). Read
# the result per docs/beta-runbook.md 6a — and read it deduped BY PERSON.
IP_PAYWALL_GATE=1
IP_PAYWALL_PRICE_USD=39
IP_PAYWALL_FREE_ROUNDS=3
IP_PAYWALL_FREE_PLANS=3
IP_PAYWALL_PAID_ROUNDS=4

# --- Stripe billing (billing.ts) ------------------------------------------
# All three together or none. Unset = billing off: the gate still works and
# manual comps still work, there is just nothing to buy.
#
# Use a RESTRICTED key (rk_), not a secret key. Least privilege: write on
# Checkout Sessions, Customers, Billing Portal Sessions; read on Subscriptions
# and Prices. Rotate it if anyone with access departs.
#
# The webhook endpoint is https://zenkai.run/api/stripe/webhook — register it
# in the Stripe Dashboard and paste the signing secret below. It is
# deliberately the one /api/ route that does not require a login, because
# Stripe sends no JWT; the signature is its authentication.
#
# TAX: US/EU customers need Stripe Tax AND an active registration. Enabling
# automatic_tax without one collects nothing and reports no error.
STRIPE_API_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_PRICE_ID=

# --- PostHog analytics (posthog.ts) ---------------------------------------
# Project key (phc_ — PUBLIC, ships to every browser; a personal phx_ key
# refuses to boot). Unset = analytics off, box byte-identical.
#
# COMMENTED on purpose: push-env.sh ships every uncommented IP_ line of this
# template verbatim, and a placeholder value here would refuse to boot at the
# prefix check. Uncomment WITH the real key, then re-run push-env.
# IP_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...
# IP_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
#
# Round-interior replay (IDE/editor/transcript/test output) stays BLOCKED
# unless this is 1. Do not flip it on the live box without measuring typing
# latency in a real round first — docs/posthog-setup.md has the procedure.
# IP_POSTHOG_REPLAY_ROUND=1
